ly Phi^2. k reads, so 2k bit queries after compilation, against the row's one bit query per D. Constant only.","open_assumptions":["1<=k"],"premises":[],"reached":true,"relation":"unassessed","review_evidence":"legacy_unbound","reviewed_by":"ai:truth-auditor","reviewed_relation":"partial","reviewed_route":"same","route":"unassessed","wrapper_comparison_evidence":"not_run"}],"ledger_history":{"added_in_review":false,"adjudication_findings":[],"earlier_ledger_wording":null,"wording_changed":false},"original_statement_sha256":"1ce97979ffc9963d91470bec06ed87fe9a7c7051a5049a7be983f02d779b32f0","passages":["forr_quantum","CAT-claim-proj-prob"],"presentation":{"body":"Prepare $u$, apply $D_{z_1}H\\cdots HD_{z_k}$ from right to left, and measure the projection onto $u$. Each sign diagonal uses one bit query through phase kickback; $H$ and the projection use no queries. The success probability is exactly $\\Phi^2$, at least $\\delta^2$ on inputs with value one and at most $\\delta^2/4$ on inputs with value zero.","body_plain":"Prepare u, apply D(z₁)H⋯HD(zₖ) from right to left, and measure the projection onto u. Each sign diagonal uses one bit query through phase kickback; H and the projection use no queries. The success probability is exactly Φ², at least δ² on inputs with value one and at most δ²/4 on inputs with value zero.","statement_sha256":"1ce97979ffc9963d91470bec06ed87fe9a7c7051a5049a7be983f02d779b32f0","title":"The projection succeeds with probability $\\Phi^2$","title_plain":"The projection succeeds with probability Φ²"},"review_scope":{"compared_text":"maintained_ledger_statement","leading_matches":[{"declaration":"QuarticQuery.Paper.construction_projection_test","file":"lean/QuarticQuery/Paper/ConstructionForrelationQuantum.lean"}],"relation_origin":"authored_review","semantic_examples":"none_indexed","type_and_axioms_origin":"compiled_lean_environment"},"section":"2.1","semantic_probes":[],"source_line":176,"statement":"Prepare u, apply D_{z_1} H ... H D_{z_k} right to left, measure the projection onto u. Each D uses one bit query (phase kickback), H and the projection use none. Success probability is exactly Phi^2: >=delta^2 on 1-inputs, <=delta^2/4 on 0-inputs.","statement_sha256":"1ce97979ffc9963d91470bec06ed87fe9a7c7051a5049a7be983f02d779b32f0"}
